<h2>Access levels and roles</h2>
<p>
  Everyone in a workspace is an <strong>owner</strong>, an <strong>admin</strong>
  or a <strong>member</strong>. Owners and admins can do everything. What a member can do comes
  from their <strong>roles</strong>.
</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Level</th><th>Can</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Owner</td>
      <td>Everything. The person who created the workspace; can't be removed.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Admin</td>
      <td>Everything, including plan &amp; billing and making other people admins.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Member</td>
      <td>
        What their roles allow. See <.link navigate="/help/roles-and-permissions">Roles &amp; permissions</.link>.
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2>Inviting people</h2>
<p>
  Admins invite from <.link navigate="/settings/users">Settings → Users</.link>. Invitations are
  valid for 14 days and can be revoked until they're accepted. New members get the default roles
  (normally <em>Team member</em>); click <strong>Roles</strong>
  next to someone to change them. Admins
  switch people between member and admin with the picker; the bin icon removes them.
</p>

<h2>Seeing the workspace as someone else</h2>
<p>
  To check what a teammate sees, or help them with a problem, open
  <.link navigate="/settings/users">Settings → Users</.link>
  (or their employee page) and click <strong>Impersonate</strong>. You're signed in as them until you
  click <strong>Stop impersonating</strong>
  in the dark banner at the top. Owners can impersonate admins and members; admins can impersonate
  members only. Every impersonation is recorded in the audit log.
</p>

<h2>Branches</h2>
<p>
  If your business has several locations, open
  <.link navigate="/settings/branches">Settings → Branches</.link>
  and tick <strong>We have several branches</strong>, then add each branch with a short code
  (e.g. NBO, MBA). Every team starts with a default branch, <em>Head office</em>.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    Quotes, orders, invoices, requests for quotation, purchase orders, bills, expense claims,
    production orders, employees and warehouses get a <strong>Branch</strong>
    field. Documents made from another (an order from a quote, a bill from a purchase order)
    keep its branch.
  </li>
  <li>
    Journal entries follow their document's branch, so the
    <.link navigate="/accounting/reports">profit &amp; loss, balance sheet and trial balance</.link>
    can be run for one branch or all of them.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Seats</h2>
<p>
  Your plan may include a number of <strong>seats</strong>. Members and open invitations both use a seat.
  When all seats are taken, new invitations are refused until you free a seat or move to a bigger plan.
</p>

<h2>Plan &amp; billing</h2>
<p>
  Admins can see the workspace's plan, seat usage, current billing period and invoices under <.link navigate="/settings/billing">Settings → Plan &amp; billing</.link>.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>The monthly price is the plan's price per seat × your number of members.</li>
  <li>New workspaces start with a free trial; the end date is shown on the billing page.</li>
  <li>
    Set the <strong>billing contact</strong> email that should receive Zippiker's invoices.
  </li>
  <li>
    To change plan, click <strong>Request this plan</strong>. The Zippiker team confirms the change
    and applies it, usually within one business day.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Modules</h2>
<p>
  CRM, Sales, Purchasing, Inventory, HR and Accounting are modules. Your plan decides which are switched on. A module that's
  off disappears from the sidebar, but its data is kept: switch it back on and everything is still there.
</p>
